# Deny everything, then re-admit only what the two Dockerfiles actually COPY.
#
# An allowlist rather than a list of things to exclude: the repository root holds .git, and a
# build context that carries it puts the full history one stray `COPY . .` away from the webapp
# root -- which is precisely what the scanners hitting /.git/config every day are looking for.
# A denylist protects against the paths someone thought to name; this protects against the ones
# nobody did. Adding a COPY without adding it here fails the build loudly, which is the safe
# direction to fail.
#
# Both images build from the repository root (see .github/workflows/publish-images.yml and
# docker-compose.yaml), so this one file governs both.
*

# docker/app/Dockerfile
!target/simis-cms.war
!target/simis-cms-ssrf-pin-resolver.jar
!docker/app/conf/server.xml
!docker/app/conf/setenv.sh
!docker/app/applicationinsights.json
!docker/app/imagemagick-policy.xml

# docker/db/Dockerfile
!docker/db/init.sql
